.TH DCTEST 1
.SH NAME
dctest \- regression test for dc(1)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dctest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.I Dctest
loads
.BR /p9/dis/dc.dis 's
in-process test seam,
.BR runstring(prog) ,
and checks a representative subset of the programs used to develop
.IR dc (1)
against golden output: arithmetic, the precision/scale rules for
.BR + / - / * / / ,
square root, registers, and stack operations
.RB ( p ", " n ", " f ", " c ", " d ", " r ).
Every expected string was checked once against
.BR /usr/bin/dc ,
the host's real
.IR dc .
.PP
Prints one line per failure to standard error, a final
.IR N " passed, " N " failed"
summary to standard output, and exits with a non-nil status if
anything failed.
.SH SOURCE
.B /p9/cmd/dctest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR dc (1)
.SH BUGS
Runs
.I dc
in-process via its
.B runstring
seam, not as a spawned subprocess reading real files and standard
input/output \(em so it does not exercise
.IR dc 's
own
.BR init ,
argument parsing
.RB ( -e / -f ),
or file I/O at all.
